Subject: [PATCH] local: wifi: ath12k: split 6 GHz discovery scans on WCN7850

A trace on the Yoga Slim 7x with scan-priority fix 0232 shows a successful
hardware scan taking 8.976505 seconds after s2idle. Userspace requests
NL80211_SCAN_FLAG_COLOCATED_6GHZ, but the scan covers 101 channels:
13 in 2.4 GHz, 28 in 5 GHz and 60 in 6 GHz. There is no post-scan
userspace delay or retry accounting for the latency.

Enable cfg80211's split 6 GHz scan handling for single-radio, tri-band
WCN7850. With the colocated-AP flag, cfg80211 scans legacy bands first and
then selects 6 GHz preferred scanning channels plus channels reported in
reduced neighbor reports. Requests without that flag retain the full
requested channel coverage. Do not shorten dwell or change country rules.

Follow Qualcomm's ChromiumOS ath11k split-scan sequencing: defer initial
11d discovery until the 6 GHz part is submitted. Otherwise firmware can
run country discovery between the two host scan parts. Keeping 11d in
PREPARING also lets 0232 send MEDIUM priority for both parts. Preserve the
existing 11d start on an unsuccessful host-scan submission.

Like that implementation, a successful legacy-only scan on a split-scan
wiphy leaves initial 11d discovery pending until a later 6 GHz scan. This
must be considered when testing band-restricted discovery. The measured
NetworkManager reconnect path requests all three bands.

Log the channel count of each submitted part for the next hardware test.
The measured 60-channel 6 GHz list has 15 PSC channels; eliminating 45
70-ms dwells could save about 3.15 seconds before RNR additions and scan
scheduling overhead. That is an estimate, not a tested WCN7850 result.

Based on the split-scan design by Manikanta Pubbisetty for WCN6750:
https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel-rebase-patches/+/eb41b7da5ebc5eea36f59356919c78d1d80b19ec/4382f958e7c6f76ee4ac49480fde23bc7c6fa3b5bb190e615fc02f3e.patch
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
@@ -5728,6 +5728,9 @@
 	}
 
 	ath12k_dbg(ar->ab, ATH12K_DBG_MAC, "mac scan started");
+	if (hw->wiphy->flags & WIPHY_FLAG_SPLIT_SCAN_6GHZ)
+		ath12k_info(ar->ab, "scan: split part 6ghz=%u channels=%u\n",
+			    req->scan_6ghz, n_channels);
 
 	/* Add a margin to account for event/command processing */
 	ieee80211_queue_delayed_work(ath12k_ar_to_hw(ar), &ar->scan.timeout,
@@ -5740,9 +5743,14 @@
 		kfree(arg);
 	}
 
+	/* Keep country discovery from delaying the second half of a split scan.
+	 * Leave 11d PREPARING so both parts get the initial MEDIUM priority.
+	 */
 	if (ar->state_11d == ATH12K_11D_PREPARING &&
 	    ahvif->vdev_type == WMI_VDEV_TYPE_STA &&
-	    ahvif->vdev_subtype == WMI_VDEV_SUBTYPE_NONE)
+	    ahvif->vdev_subtype == WMI_VDEV_SUBTYPE_NONE &&
+	    (ret || !(hw->wiphy->flags & WIPHY_FLAG_SPLIT_SCAN_6GHZ) ||
+	     req->scan_6ghz))
 		ath12k_mac_11d_scan_start(ar, arvif->vdev_id);
 
 	return ret;
@@ -14862,8 +14870,11 @@
 	if (ah->num_radio == 1 &&
 	    wiphy->bands[NL80211_BAND_2GHZ] &&
 	    wiphy->bands[NL80211_BAND_5GHZ] &&
-	    wiphy->bands[NL80211_BAND_6GHZ])
+	    wiphy->bands[NL80211_BAND_6GHZ]) {
 		ieee80211_hw_set(hw, SINGLE_SCAN_ON_ALL_BANDS);
+		if (ab->hw_rev == ATH12K_HW_WCN7850_HW20)
+			wiphy->flags |= WIPHY_FLAG_SPLIT_SCAN_6GHZ;
+	}
 
 	ieee80211_hw_set(hw, SIGNAL_DBM);
 	ieee80211_hw_set(hw, SUPPORTS_PS);
